Ladybird places the closing edges of an inline box before the next
item when its final text node is empty and produces no caret fragment.
This retains padding, border, and margin space before following text
for an empty generated-content box. Empty text in an editing host or
text control still receives its caret fragment and consumes its edges.

Blink’s LineBreaker::HandleCloseTag adds ComputeInlineEndSize to the
line position before processing the following item. WebKit’s Line::
appendInlineBoxEnd adds a closing run and advances the content width.
Gecko’s nsInlineFrame::ReflowFrames includes the end padding and border
when completing the inline frame, even without text. Ladybird matches
that ordering. Chrome 157 confirmed both ::before and ::after, the
combined-edge case, and the whitespace control.
